/-
Johnson/Desc/Ok/PlanWritten/CutLit.lean: the cut of the proof file's IOP as written in Lean into
sub-protocols, at the full size, written out: three lists, one for each chain. Data alone.

A row, of one sub-protocol: its name · its place ⟨chain, link, number in the link, kind⟩ · how many
rounds it declares · the length of its field `oracles` · the rounds that tell a tree: (the round's
number, from 0, the trees ⟨log-length, words of a symbol, tenants⟩), a tenant being ⟨main words,
mask words, degree, whether it has an out-of-domain (OOD) sample, the groups that it joins⟩ · its
field `before`: (chain, the message's number in its chain's order of sending).

Whence. Printed by a program off `ProofFile.onlineDescription` at the goals' stored full-size public files
(`VerifierAndGoals.storedPublicFiles`, Ladder/Stored.lean), by Lean's evaluator, and laid into Lean's notation by a second
program. NO THEOREM SAYS THAT THESE ARE THAT VALUE's ROWS: the test of CutTest.lean compares them at
a run.

  `cutFirstFull`   358 rows · `cutSharedFull`  12 rows · `cutSecondFull`  4 rows

-/
